<h1>Lock in Space</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from the</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>tree context menu &gt; Lock in Space</b></span></i><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Lock in Space</span> <span class="Command">command locks single or multiple entities or groups so that they won't be affected when updating the Current CS. It is available for all entities with the exception of transformations and view positions.</span></p>
<p>In some cases it is necessary to register objects (meshes, scan data, etc.) to a CAD model. This way it must be set which entities will not be affected by the transformation, i.e. the CAD model and eventually its nominal datum entities. In order to do that, mark these entities (by left-click on their names in the Entities tree while holding Shift or Ctrl buttons.) Then right-click and select <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Lock in Space</b></span> command. This will mark them as locked in the World CS. A small push-pin will appear on their icons:</p>
<p class="whs4"><img src="Images/Locked.gif" width="220px" height="284px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></p>
<p>When current CS is updated with some transformation all entities in the scene with the exception of locked ones are affected.</p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2"><span style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Example</u></span></a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP166720093" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="Images/Lock_example.gif" width="437px" height="186px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p>Locking can be performed even when there is already an active transformation. In this case there are three options:</p>
<p><img src="Images/Lock_buttons.gif" width="423px" height="100px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="font-weight:bold;">Lock where it is <span style="font-weight:normal;">- the entities are locked at their current position and any other changes (back to World CS or updating with another transformation) will not affect them.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="font-weight:bold;">Back to WCS and lock <span style="font-weight:normal;">- the entities are set back to the World CS and then locked.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="font-weight:bold;">Cancel <span style="font-weight:normal;">- cancels this dialog and leaves the entities at their current state.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Use"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Use</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB" class="Command">Lock in Space</span> <span lang="EN-GB">to set the reference (nominal) objects when register.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><a href="javascript:void(0);" onclick="var e; if (parseInt(navigator.appVersion)&gt;=4){e=event;} if (parseInt(navigator.appVersion) &gt;=2 &amp;&amp; typeof(PopupMenu_Invoke) == 'function') PopupMenu_Invoke(e,'','Unlock','Unlock.htm','Unlock','../Macros/Commands/Unlock.htm','Update Current CS','Update_Current_CS.htm');return false;" title=""><img src="../add_on/ss_btn_see_also.gif" border="0" height="17" width="60" alt=""></a></span></p>
